[ti:Golden Hours]
[ar:FIRST SUMMER]
[length:00:59]
[00:05.00]We ran where the tall grass grew
[00:11.20]Red flowers caught against our shoes
[00:17.40]Stayed outside past half-past nine
[00:23.60]Like summer had forgotten time
[00:31.00]We didn't know it was the last
[00:37.20]Golden hours moving fast
[00:43.40]The whole wide world was waiting there
[00:49.60]We were running without a care
